---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { site } from '../../content';
const path = "/compare/sendlane-vs-klaviyo";
const title = "Sendlane vs Klaviyo for Shopify: 2026 Comparison";
const desc = "Acquisition continuity versus rebuilding your Shopify data workflows. Practical evaluation criteria, current product sources and migration checks.";
const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "Does acquisition mean my account will change?",
    "answer": "Ask the account team for written product, contract and support continuity terms. The acquisition announcement alone does not settle individual accounts."
  },
  {
    "question": "What should a migration quote include?",
    "answer": "Request flow inventory, rebuild responsibilities, exclusions, validation, escalation and rollback deliverables."
  },
  {
    "question": "How should I compare costs?",
    "answer": "Use equivalent audience, send volume, peak season and service scope in current quotes. No fixed supplier prices are assumed here."
  },
  {
    "question": "Which Shopify events matter here?",
    "answer": "For the proposed furniture example, payment, fulfillment, cancellation and refund behavior determine safe follow-up."
  },
  {
    "question": "Can Sequenzy be considered?",
    "answer": "Yes, as a commerce email candidate after checking required events, suppression and ownership; no automatic saving is claimed."
  },
  {
    "question": "What about SMS?",
    "answer": "Confirm account access, eligible countries, consent handling and cross-channel exclusions separately before enabling texts."
  },
  {
    "question": "What should I check before a sale?",
    "answer": "Inspect deadlines and scheduled messages for gift buyers, recent purchasers and refunded orders."
  },
  {
    "question": "What decides whether to switch?",
    "answer": "A maintainable journey and a concrete support or operating benefit must justify migration costs and risks."
  }
];
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
  <section class="container py-14 md:py-20">
    <nav class="mb-8 text-sm"><a class="link" href="/compare">Comparisons</a></nav>
    <header class="max-w-4xl">
      <p class="badge">Head-to-head</p>
      <h1 class="hero-title mt-5">Sendlane vs Klaviyo for Shopify</h1>
      <p class="mt-7 text-xl">Acquisition continuity versus rebuilding your Shopify data workflows.</p>
      <p class="mt-5">Source review updated November 24, 2026. This is a documented-scope comparison and proposed evaluation, not a hands-on trial or revenue benchmark. Account access, exact connector behavior and current quotes remain to be verified.</p>
    </header>
    <article class="prose-shopify mt-14 max-w-4xl">
      <h2>The acquisition changes the decision</h2>
      <p>Privy acquired Sendlane in 2026. Its announcement emphasizes human support and a connected ecommerce platform. Existing Sendlane customers should first obtain their account transition terms; new buyers should ask which product, contract and support team they are actually buying. This is a continuity decision as well as a feature comparison.</p>
      <p><a class="link" href="https://www.privy.com/blog/privy-acquires-sendlane">Primary product documentation</a></p>
      <h2>What Klaviyo documents</h2>
      <p>Klaviyo publishes a detailed Shopify event reference, including checkout, order and storefront activity. That gives an evaluator a concrete field map to audit rather than a promise of maximum depth. Availability still depends on integration and tracking configuration.</p>
      <p><a class="link" href="https://help.klaviyo.com/hc/en-us/articles/115005080447">Primary product documentation</a></p>
      <h2>Proposed home-goods cutover rehearsal</h2>
      <p>Use a hypothetical made-to-order furniture catalog with long delivery lead times. Build a purchase follow-up that sends care information after fulfillment, not merely after payment. Then cancel one order and partially refund another. Inspect whether each queued message still makes sense. These are proposed checks; no merchant outcomes or build times were measured.</p>
      <h2>Buy support as a deliverable</h2>
      <p>Ask the Sendlane/Privy team to list who rebuilds existing flows, who validates exclusions and who handles a failed sync. Specify acceptance criteria for the furniture journey: correct variant, correct fulfillment milestone, no promotion after cancellation. Request a named escalation path and agreed rollback procedure. Do not assume quarterly reviews, free migration or a completion date are included.</p>
      <h2>Stay or switch on dependencies</h2>
      <p>Inventory Klaviyo filters, custom metrics, catalog references and agency-maintained flows before requesting a competing quote. If those dependencies work and your team can maintain them, switching needs a concrete benefit beyond a simpler demo. If maintenance has stalled, compare the cost of repairing the current account with contracted migration help. Neither choice establishes better revenue without a controlled measurement.</p>
      <h2>Peak-sale safety</h2>
      <p>For a hypothetical gift campaign, preview recent purchasers, gift recipients and refunded orders separately. Edit one shipping deadline and inspect scheduled messages before launch. Keep the original sender available for rollback without leaving duplicate automations active. Support promises should include what happens when a sale-week edit fails, not just initial onboarding.</p>
      <h2>Cost and other candidates</h2>
      <p>Request current quotes using the same eligible audience, monthly sends, seasonal peak, SMS destinations and service deliverables. Include rebuilding, training and overlap costs. Sequenzy is another commerce email candidate if its required events and stop conditions pass your rehearsal; it is not an automatic saving or replacement for contracted support.</p>
      <p><a class="link" href="https://www.sequenzy.com/features/shopify-integration">Primary product documentation</a></p>
      <h2>Decision rule</h2>
      <p>Choose the option whose documented event mapping and assigned operating owner can maintain the fulfillment journey. Resolve acquisition terms before committing to Sendlane/Privy. Keep Klaviyo if the repair plan meets your requirements more economically than migration. Record unresolved field mappings as blockers, rather than hiding them behind a platform winner.</p>
    </article>
      <div class="mt-10 max-w-4xl text-sm">
        <p class="font-black text-white">Related comparisons</p>
        <p class="mt-2">
          <a class="link" href="/compare/drip-vs-sendlane">Drip vs Sendlane</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/compare/klaviyo-vs-omnisend">Klaviyo vs Omnisend</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/compare/sequenzy-vs-klaviyo">Sequenzy vs Klaviyo</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/for/home-goods">Email apps for home goods stores</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/use-cases/abandoned-cart">Abandoned cart playbook</a>
        </p>
      </div>
  </section>
  <FaqSection faqs={faqs} title="Sendlane vs Klaviyo FAQ" />
</BaseLayout>
